# Root .gitignore blanket-excludes *.pt/*.onnx/*.onnx.data ("keep training
# reproducible instead of committing weights blindly") — a sound policy for
# real-scale model weights. This directory's Phase 2A spike artifacts are a
# deliberate, narrow exception: they're tiny (~40KB checkpoint, ~36KB ONNX),
# and docs/repair/showboat-ml/ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md's acceptance test
# (rankerIntegration.test.ts) depends on the ONNX file existing to prove the
# pipeline works without requiring every contributor to stand up a Python +
# PyTorch environment just to run `npm test`. Reproduction commands are in
# README.md regardless. Not a precedent for committing real-scale weights —
# Phase 2C+ artifacts follow the root policy.
!artifacts/run1/checkpoint.pt
!artifacts/run1/showboat-ranker.onnx

# Phase 2C dataset generation output (all profiles, including smoke): fully
# reproducible from code + master seed in well under a minute (smoke) to a
# few hours (full) — see phase2c/gen_dataset_v3.ts and DATASET_DESIGN.md.
# Even smoke's tiny fixture is ~500KB of generated NDJSON; regenerating on
# demand (`npm run ranker:gen-smoke`) is cheaper than tracking it, and its
# determinism (byte-identical dataset_hash across runs) is exactly what
# makes that safe to rely on instead of committing the output.
phase2c/data/
